TITLE:: SynthVVST
summary:: Synthesizer V VST wrapper with caching and multi-voice expansion
categories:: SynthV
related:: Classes/SynthV, Classes/P

DESCRIPTION::
SynthVVST wraps the Synthesizer V Studio VST plugin for real-time vocal synthesis. It generates an SVP project file and FXP preset, loads them into a VST instance, and provides transport control for playback.

Features include build caching (identical params reuse the same VST), automatic multi-voice expansion via SC's rank/flop idiom, phoneme morphing across languages, AI take variation, and integration with the Song system via link::Classes/P#*synthVVST::.

subsection:: Basic workflow

code::
// 1. Create with voice key and params
s = SynthVVST(\xuan2, params: (
    lyrics: "hello world how are you",
    midinote: [60, 62, 64, 65, 67],
    dur: [1, 1, 0.5, 0.5, 1],
    lag: 0.15.dup(5)
));

// 2. Optionally apply filters
s.morphPhonemes([\korean, \english, \mandarin], randomSeed: 4);

// 3. Build (generates SVP, loads VST)
s.build;

// 4. Wait for "SynthVVST: xuan2 ready" in post window, then play
s.play;

// 5. Cleanup
SynthVVST.freeAll;
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create a new SynthVVST instance. If any parameter value has code::rank > 1:: (arrays of arrays), multi-voice expansion is triggered automatically.

ARGUMENT:: voice
A Symbol key into code::SynthV.databaseLib::. Available V2 voices include code::\xuan2::, code::\uni::, code::\choirZh2::, code::\choirEn2::. V1 voices: code::\kevin::, code::\feng::, code::\an::, code::\mo::, code::\genbu::, code::\aiko::.

ARGUMENT:: params
An Event of synthesis parameters. See link::#Params reference:: below.

ARGUMENT:: version
SynthV engine version. Default code::2::.

returns:: A SynthVVST instance.

METHOD:: freeAll
Free all cached VST instances (buses, controllers) and clear the cache.

METHOD:: clearCache
Alias for code::freeAll::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: build
Generate the SVP project, write the FXP preset, and load the VST plugin. Results are cached by content -- calling build again with identical params returns instantly.

A background notification code::"SynthVVST: <voice> ready":: posts to the post window when the VST has loaded and rendering is estimated to be complete.

returns:: this

METHOD:: play
Start VST transport and route audio through an optional processing function. Automatically stops transport and frees the synth after the duration completes. Safe to call multiple times -- previous cleanup routines are cancelled.

ARGUMENT:: func
A signal processing function applied to the VST output. Default is identity (passthrough).

code::
// with reverb and panning
s.play({ |sig| FreeVerb.ar(sig, 0.3, 1) => Pan2.ar(_, 0) });

// with volume scaling
s.play({ |sig| sig * 0.5 });
::

ARGUMENT:: tail
Extra seconds of playback after the last note. Default code::1::.

METHOD:: morphPhonemes
Apply cross-language phoneme substitution cipher to lyrics. Modifies params in place. In multi-voice mode, each voice gets a different random seed (code::randomSeed + voiceIndex::).

ARGUMENT:: languages
Array of language Symbols to draw phonemes from. Sorted internally. Options: code::\english::, code::\mandarin::, code::\korean::, code::\japanese::.

ARGUMENT:: randomSeed
Integer seed for deterministic phoneme substitution. Default code::12345::.

returns:: this (chainable)

METHOD:: buses
Access the raw audio bus(es).

returns:: A Bus (single voice) or Array of Bus (multi-voice).

METHOD:: isMulti
returns:: Boolean. code::true:: if multi-voice expansion is active.

METHOD:: voices
returns:: Array of per-voice param Events, or code::nil:: if single voice.

METHOD:: params
returns:: The params Event (in multi-voice mode, returns the first voice's params).

METHOD:: synthV
returns:: The underlying SynthV instance (single voice) or Array of SynthV instances (multi-voice).

SECTION:: Params reference

The code::params:: Event controls all aspects of the synthesis. Required keys are code::lyrics::, code::midinote::, and code::dur::.

subsection:: Core params

definitionList::
## lyrics
|| String of space-separated words. Use code::"r":: for rests (filtered out). Number of words should match number of notes.
## midinote
|| Array of MIDI note numbers (integers). One per note.
## dur
|| Array of durations in beats. Determines the number of notes created.
## lag
|| Array of onset offsets in beats. Typically code::0.15.dup(n)::. Uses clipAt for short arrays.
## legato
|| Array of legato multipliers for note duration. Default code::1::. Uses clipAt.
::

subsection:: Voice and expression

definitionList::
## vocalMode
|| Symbol or Array of Symbols. Sets the vocal mode preset. e.g. code::\Soft::, code::\Belt::, code::\Clear::. Use code::SynthV.modes(\voiceKey):: to list available modes.
## singers
|| Integer. Number of choir stems (for choir voices like code::\choirZh2::, code::\choirEn2::).
## spacing
|| Float. Choir seating separation. Default code::0.7::.
## language
|| Symbol. Override the voice's default language.
## phoneset
|| Symbol. Override the voice's default phoneset.
::

subsection:: AI takes

definitionList::
## aiTakes
|| Integer or Array of per-note take IDs. code::0:: = default rendering, code::1+:: = AI variation with deterministic seeds derived from code::(takeId * 1000 + noteIndex)::. Short arrays use clipAt.
::

code::
// all notes use AI take 1
(aiTakes: 1)

// per-note: default for first 4, variation for last 4
(aiTakes: [0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 1])

// short array: note 0 default, notes 1+ use take 2
(aiTakes: [0, 2])
::

subsection:: Choir spread

Per-note attributes controlling choir voice dispersion. Use clipAt for short arrays.

definitionList::
## pitchSpread
|| Float. Pitch dispersion across choir voices. Default code::0.15::.
## startSpread
|| Float. Note start time dispersion. Default code::0.5::.
## endSpread
|| Float. Phrase tail dispersion. Default code::0.35::.
::

subsection:: Envelopes

Time-varying parameters accept an Env value:

definitionList::
## toneShift || Env
## pitchDelta || Env
## voicing || Env
## tension || Env
## vibratoEnv || Env
## loudness || Env
## breathiness || Env
## gender || Env
## mouthOpening || Env
::

Vocal mode envelopes use the prefix code::vm:: followed by the mode name:
code::
(vmSoft: Env([0, 100, 0], [2, 2]))
::

subsection:: Pitch control

definitionList::
## pitchTake
|| Integer. Active pitch take ID.
## pitchExpression
|| Float or Array. Expression value written to all pitch takes.
## defaultVibratoDepth
|| Float. Default vibrato depth.
::

SECTION:: Multi-voice expansion

When any param value has code::rank > 1:: (an array of arrays), SynthVVST automatically creates multiple internal VST instances. Scalar and rank-1 params are shared across voices; rank-2 params are distributed one per voice.

code::
// Two voices with different pitches, same lyrics/rhythm
s = SynthVVST(\xuan2, params: (
    lyrics: "hello world how are you",
    midinote: [[60, 62, 64, 65, 67], [65, 67, 69, 70, 72]],  // rank 2 -> 2 voices
    dur: [1, 1, 0.5, 0.5, 1],  // rank 1 -> shared
    lag: 0.15.dup(5)
));
s.build;

// play mixes all voices through func
s.play({ |sig| sig * 0.5 });

// access individual buses
s.buses;  // -> Array of 2 Bus objects
::

Multi-voice expansion also works with code::aiTakes:::

code::
// aiTakes: [[0, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1]] -> voice 1 default, voice 2 AI variation
::

SECTION:: Song integration with P.synthVVST

code::P.synthVVST:: creates a link::Classes/P:: (Part) that integrates SynthVVST into the Song system.

code::
P.synthVVST(\xuan2, take: \lead, start: \verse,
    params: { |song durs key| [
        lyrics: "hello world how are you doing today friend",
        midinote: [1, 3, 5, 4, 5, 4, 3, 2].dm(\c),
        dur: durs,
        lag: 0.15.dup(8)
    ]},
    filters: _.morphPhonemes([\korean, \english, \mandarin], randomSeed: 4),
    music: { |p b e|
        {
            e.bus
            => FreeVerb.ar(_, 0.3, 1)
            => Pan2.ar(_, 0)
        }.play
    }
);
::

subsection:: P.synthVVST arguments

definitionList::
## voice || Symbol. Voice key.
## start || Symbol or Integer. Song section name or index.
## params || Function receiving code::(song, durs, voiceKey):: and returning a flat array of key-value pairs.
## syl || Syllable count (optional).
## lag || Default lag. Default code::0::.
## music || Function receiving code::(part, bus, event)::. code::e.bus:: returns code::In.ar:: of the VST output (or Array for multi-voice). code::e.sv:: returns the SynthVVST instance.
## song || Song instance. Default code::Song.currentSong::.
## resources || Additional resources Event merged into the Part.
## filters || Function or Array of Functions applied to the SynthVVST before building. e.g. code::_.morphPhonemes(...)::
## version || SynthV engine version. Default code::2::.
## take || Symbol. Differentiates multiple parts using the same voice.
## tail || Extra seconds after last note. Default code::1::.
::

EXAMPLES::

subsection:: Basic standalone usage

code::
(
~sv = SynthVVST(\xuan2, params: (
    lyrics: "the quick brown fox jumps over",
    midinote: [60, 62, 64, 65, 67, 69],
    dur: [0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 1, 1],
    lag: 0.15.dup(6)
));
~sv.build;
)
// wait for ready message
~sv.play({ |sig| Pan2.ar(sig, 0) });
::

subsection:: With phoneme morphing

code::
(
~sv = SynthVVST(\xuan2, params: (
    lyrics: "singing across languages today",
    midinote: [60, 64, 67, 64, 60],
    dur: [1, 1, 1, 1, 2],
    lag: 0.15.dup(5)
));
~sv.morphPhonemes([\korean, \english, \mandarin], randomSeed: 42);
~sv.build;
)
~sv.play;
::

subsection:: AI take variations

code::
(
var params = (
    lyrics: "hello world how are you",
    midinote: [60, 62, 64, 65, 67],
    dur: [1, 1, 0.5, 0.5, 1],
    lag: 0.15.dup(5)
);
~default = SynthVVST(\xuan2, params: params);
~default.build;

~varied = SynthVVST(\xuan2, params: params.copy.put(\aiTakes, 1));
~varied.build;
)
~default.play;  // default rendering
~varied.play;   // AI variation
::

subsection:: Multi-voice with choir

code::
(
~choir = SynthVVST(\choirZh2, params: (
    lyrics: "la la la la",
    midinote: [[60, 64, 67, 72], [55, 59, 62, 67]],  // soprano + alto
    dur: [1, 1, 1, 2],
    lag: 0.15.dup(4),
    singers: 8,
    spacing: 0.3
));
~choir.build;
)
~choir.play({ |sig| FreeVerb.ar(sig, 0.5, 1) });

// individual bus access
~choir.buses;
::

subsection:: Cleanup

code::
SynthVVST.freeAll;  // free all cached instances
::
